00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.869 align:start position:0%
the protest against cobot 19 mandates  ended in february after 18 days when  police made arrests and seized a large  cache of weapons and ammunition anthony  olynyk jerry morin chris carbert and  chris lizack are charged with murder  conspiracy weapons offenses and mischief  according to the unsealed documents  undercover officers spoke to organizers  of the protest at smuggler's saloon  police allege olenick morin and carbert  were part of a subgroup with loose ties  to the leading organizers and that the  three participated in bringing firearms  into the coots blockade area the  documents also allege one of the  officers spoke to olenek who brought a  dump truck to the blockade and said he  was involved in security  and discussed having access to hundreds  of firearms and ammunition within coutes  key portions of the discussion with  olynyk involving a delivery believed to  be a bank of weapons remain under a  stealing order the documents also show  police were seeking a warrant to seize  papers relating to the financing of the  blockade an undercover officer allegedly  saw a man with an estimated 500 pages of  documents described as financial records  and police said conversations inside the  saloon alerted them to a finance  committee pointing to what they called a  governance structure police also wrote  that financial records will provide  evidence of people directly involved in  the blockade as well as those who  supplied money and resources making them  party to the name defense the  allegations in the newly released  documents have not been proven in court  the four accused are scheduled to stand  trial in june of 2023
 

